From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 17:14:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 58/83] contrib: port HexChat 2.10.2 (GTK+ 2 IRC client)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cross-built against the substrate GTK+ 2.x stack via substrate_sysroot.
2.10.2 is the last autotools HexChat (2.12+ is meson-only, and substrate has
no meson cross harness).

Harness:
- In-source build: HexChat's generators hardcode source-relative paths
  (make-te reads textevents.in; fe-gtk reads ../../data/*.gresource.xml),
  which out-of-source can't resolve.
- make-te (a noinst text-event generator the cross build compiles for the
  target) is rebuilt with the host gcc; the GResource step uses the host
  glib-compile-resources.
- D-Bus/libnotify/libproxy/libcanberra/isocodes/sysinfo/NLS and the Perl/
  Python plugin loaders are disabled (no ports); gtk/glib cross run-tests
  disabled.

SSL deferred: HexChat 2.10.2 reaches into OpenSSL 1.0 internals
(ssl->session->sess_cert->peer_rsa_tmp, X509->cert_info->key->algor,
X509_STORE_CTX->current_cert) that are opaque/removed in substrate's
OpenSSL 3.x, so --disable-openssl for now.

Produces /usr/bin/hexchat (2.6M); all DT_NEEDED resolve in the GTK2 stack.
Runtime: builds + links clean and the lib chain is proven (GTK2 smoke test);
a headless `hexchat -v` hangs in early startup (no crash) — full verification
needs a live X server, tracked in README.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
